<title>SPAIN: Spain Aug CPI rose 0.3 pct, yr/yr 3.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Aug CPI rose 0.3 pct, yr/yr 3.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		AUG 96    JULY 96    AUG 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change	0.3	  0.1	  0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.7	  3.7	  4.3</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.2	  0.1	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.6	  3.5	  4.9</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     AUG 96    JULY 96     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				   0.7	   0.0	4.3</p>
<p> Clothing			     0.0	   0.0	2.8</p>
<p> Housing				0.2	   0.2	3.9</p>
<p> Household goods		    0.0	   0.1	4.2</p>
<p> Medicine			     0.0	   0.1	3.6</p>
<p> Transport			    0.2	   0.2	3.4</p>
<p> Culture				0.0	   0.0	3.0</p>
<p> Other				  0.1	   0.3	3.7</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food rose 0.9 pct from the previous month (4.2 pct year-on-year) and processed food rose 0.5 (4.3 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
